  "oracle_attribution": "The three symbols are the public API of the new os/sys/process-mutex module, whose addition is the PR's entire purpose; the new test exists solely to exercise them and includes sys/process-mutex.h plus calls to init/try_lock/unlock. They are not incidental fixture helpers. At base the header and these functions are absent (verified) and PROCESS_EVENT_UNLOCKED is not defined in os/sys/process.h (PROCESS_EVENT_MAX is 0x8a, not 0x8b), so the test source cannot compile before; the PR supplies precisely the interface the test needs, and the bump of PROCESS_EVENT_MAX to 0x8b backs the PROCESS_EVENT_UNLOCKED event the unlock path posts to wake waiters.",
